	<!--
	Dynamic Quests (DynamicQuestManager, config/Custom/DynamicQuests.ini).
	Procedurally generated quests. No quest is a Java class: each template below is put together from reusable objectives, and every offer of it is
	rolled from a seed for the party that takes it. Its hunting ground and monsters come from the retail spawns around the party's level, its counts,
	champion tiers, meters and time limits from the party's size and the tier chosen (Easy, Normal, Hard, Elite), its names from the text pools.

	settings     noticeBoardNpc, heraldNpc: the custom npcs of the Notice Board and of the heralds (data/stats/npcs/custom/DynamicQuests.xml).
	board        a town with a Notice Board: town (its name), anchor (the npc it stands next to, the gatekeeper).
	monsterPool  monsters by level band (minLevel, npcId, tier), used when a quest has no hunting ground: objective pool="...".
	rewardTable  items a template's <reward table="..."> adds: id, count, minLevel/maxLevel (the quest's level), chance (percent), scaled (count x multipliers).
	itemTable    items DELIVER asks for, same attributes.
	textPool     lines a template picks from with <context key pool>, and the clue lines of INVESTIGATE (lines="...").
	requester    a kind of town npc whose requests are on the boards: title (part of the npc's title) or types (npc types), label (shown after its name).

	template id name category scope (PERSONAL | WORLD) requester (a requester kind) entryStages (stages a quest may start at, picked by its seed)
	  trigger      type = BOARD_DAILY            on every town's board each day (weight)
	                      NPC_INTERACTION        a request of a town npc of the template's requester kind, on its town's board each day (weight)
	                      TIMER                  every DynamicQuestEventInterval seconds, with chance (percent): a herald brings it to a player hunting in the
	                                             open world; a WORLD template starts around such a player
	                      WORLD_STATE            threshold kills in one hunting ground (4096x4096) within DynamicQuestAreaKillWindow seconds, with chance
	                      PLAYER_ACTION          action = KILL | LEVEL_UP, with chance per action: a herald brings it
	  eligibility  minLevel maxLevel partyMin partyMax classes (class ids) races towns (board towns) nightOnly cooldown (seconds after a completion)
	               dailyLimit (completions per account per day, 0 = only DynamicQuestAccountDailyLimit)
	  context      key pool: a line of the pool, picked by the quest's seed, fills {key} in every text (target, hostage, leader, gang, caravan,
	               expedition, item, cargo, captain, beast).
	  stage        name timeLimit (seconds at Normal, 0 = none) failOnDeath (the owner's death fails it); <text> is told when it starts.
	    objective  type + its own attributes (see the classes in model/dynamicquest/objective). Every objective takes optional="true" (adds
	               DynamicQuestOptionalBonusPercent to the reward when done), text="..." (its line in the quest window) and bonus:
	               HP_ABOVE:n | METER_ABOVE:n | FAST:n | NO_DEATHS (counts as an optional objective when it holds).
	               KILL        source = QUEST (spawned: count, at, spawnMin/Max, tierBonus, title, named, guards, escalate FLEE|LEADER|FLEE_LEADER)
	                                    | AREA (the hunting ground's monsters) | LEVEL (any of the quest's level) | NPC (npcIds)
	               CULL        count perPlayer max radius percent tierBonus alphaTitle alphaTierBonus spreadMin spreadMax
	               COLLECT     name count chance source = AREA | LEVEL | NODE (nodeNpc, radius, gatherTime) itemId (a real item too)
	               DELIVER     table kinds | items ("id:count,..."): handed over at a Notice Board
	               ESCORT      escortee dest (TOWN | ROUTE) legs legMin legMax ambushCount meter drain abandonRange lostTime at
	               INVESTIGATE clues clueNpc searchTime at firstMin firstMax spacingMin spacingMax lines ambushChance ambushCount
	               DEFEND      target waves waveCount waveInterval prep boss bossTierBonus bossTitle meter drain at
	               INTERACT    npc at spawnMin spawnMax dialog button line
	               REACH       dest (TOWN_FAR | TOWN_NEAR | HOME | AREA | LAST) radius noTeleport minDistance maxDistance ambushEvery ambushCount
	               DESTROY     nests nestNpc spawnEvery maxAlive burnTime radius broodTitle broodTierBonus
	               at = AREA (the hunting ground) | LAST (where the previous step ended) | NEAR (the owner).
	    on         event = SUCCESS | FAILURE | TIMEOUT, action = NEXT | STAGE (target) | COMPLETE | FAIL | FOLLOW_UP (target template) |
	               ESCALATE (max, extraTime), chance (percent; the first rule that rolls is taken), text. Without a rule: SUCCESS goes on, the rest fail.
	  reward       exp (percent of the EXP from the quest's level to the next) sp (SP per EXP) adenaPerLevel table + its own items.
	  text         key: title (board name), offer (board text), success, failTime, failText, failLogout, failDeath, failEscalate, failStart,
	               heraldLine, worldAnnounce, worldSuccess, worldFail.
	-->

